    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nRunning `/search1/;/search2` with ui2 enabled gives an error:\n```\nvim.schedule callback: ...0.12.5/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua:482: attempt to concatenate a nil value\nstack traceback:\n\t...0.12.5/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua:482: in function 'handler'\n\tvim/_core/ui2:158: in function 'fn'\n\t[string \"vim/_core/editor\"]:409: in function <[string \"vim/_core/editor\"]:408>\n```\n\nThe error points to these lines:\n```lua\n479    -- Extract only the search_count, not the entered search command.\n480    -- Match any of search.c:cmdline_search_stat():' [(x | >x | ?)/(y | >y | ??)]'\n481    content = { content[#content] }\n482    content[2][2] = content[1][2]:match('W? %[>?%d*%??/>?%d*%?*%]') .. '  '\n483    M.virt.last[M.virt.idx.search] = content\n484    M.virt.last[M.virt.idx.cmd] = { { 2, (' '):rep(11) } }\n485    set_virttext('last', 'cmd')\n```\nThe error also happens with `/search1/;?search2`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean\n:= vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { \"odd line\", \"even line\", \"odd line\", \"even line\" })\n/even/;/even\n# observe that no error is thrown\ngg<C-l>\n:lua require(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable()\n/even/;/even\n# observe error in the cmdline. g< to see it fully\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo error would be thrown with ui2 enabled.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nnightly commit 85c264b7d0337ab9ae9c94437b62b545481bce3c\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, no ui2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS unstable\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nKitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nnixpkgs",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I can take a look at this `ui2` search-offset error. The repro points to `messages.lua` assuming the search-count text is present, then concatenating the result of `:match(...)` even when the `/even/;/even` command shape leaves that match nil. I will reproduce with `nvim --clean`, enable `vim._core.ui2`, and check whether the fix should guard the match result or parse the search-count message differently when a second search pattern is chained after `;`. I will include the exact `/even/;/even` case as a regression test if it fits the existing UI/message tests.",
